        <mxCell id="l2note" value="&lt;b&gt;Read this way:&lt;/b&gt; everything below the engine is snodo's actual product — protocol compilation, capability binding, audit, sessions, isolation. &lt;b&gt;Coder Adapters&lt;/b&gt; is an integration seam, not a core competence, and it is the only container with several implementations that must independently satisfy the engine's expectations. That is where the drift is." style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;" vertex="1" parent="1">
