        <mxCell id="v3find" value="&lt;b&gt;The empirical finding this subsystem has to answer for&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Across two projects and a full week, &lt;b&gt;every defect that was caught was caught by `quality`&lt;/b&gt; — the only validator that executes anything. The read-only judges passed all of them, each with a detailed, confident, well-cited justification.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;That is not an argument for deleting judges. It is an argument that a judge earns its place only where nothing executable can answer the question: does this contradict a recorded decision? does this leak personal data? was the task actually completed? Everywhere else, spend the budget on a command.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;`acceptance` is the deliberate test of that line — it asks a question no command can answer. &lt;b&gt;It has not yet been observed rejecting anything.&lt;/b&gt; Until it has, it is an unproven fourth judge, not a closed gap.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF2CC;strokeColor=#D6B656;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="710" width="1130" height="160" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>

  <diagram id="c4-l3-foundation" name="L3 · Foundation / Protocol">
    <mxGraphModel dx="1600" dy="1000" grid="0" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="1600" pageHeight="900" math="0" shadow="0">
      <root>
        <mxCell id="0" />
        <mxCell id="1" parent="0" />

        <mxCell id="f3t" value="L3 · Foundation / Protocol Layer  (snodo.compiler · snodo.protocols · snodo.infrastructure)" style="text;html=1;fontSize=20;fontStyle=1;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="20" width="1200" height="30" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3s" value="This is snodo's actual product surface: policy as data, capability bound to mode, and an audit trail that cannot be quietly rewritten." style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;fontColor=#555555;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="48" width="1200" height="20" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="f3cA" value="Protocol compilation" style="rounded=0;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#D0D0D0;dashed=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=6;fontSize=11;fontColor=#999999;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="90" width="480" height="340" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3mod" value="&lt;b&gt;models.py&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;Protocol · Mode (tools, validators, transitions, per-mode overrides) · Validator (type, phase, criteria, severity_cap, tools, judges_spec) · ExecutionConfig (max_recovery_depth, max_total_fix_attempts, auto_merge, prepare_command) · exclusive_tools&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#85BBF0;strokeColor=#5D82A8;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="120" width="440" height="125" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3ver" value="&lt;b&gt;verifier.py — well-formedness at load&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;WF1′ exclusivity on approval-conferring tools (approve, merge) — relaxed from total tool disjointness, ADR 017 · WF2–WF5 · a malformed protocol never runs&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#85BBF0;strokeColor=#5D82A8;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="262" width="440" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3tpl" value="&lt;b&gt;protocols/templates/&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;solo · team · 2+n · greenfield (decide→scaffold→build) · bugfix-surgeon · feature-warden · intent&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#85BBF0;strokeColor=#5D82A8;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="60" y="368" width="440" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="f3cB" value="Governance — the invariants" style="rounded=0;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#D0D0D0;dashed=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=6;fontSize=11;fontColor=#999999;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="550" y="90" width="480" height="340" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3tok" value="&lt;b&gt;tokens.py — INV1 token integrity&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;TokenIssuer, JWT. A validation token binds a validated proposal to the execution that follows, and is consumed at the dispatch boundary. SNODO_TOKEN_SECRET must be shared across engine ↔ MCP processes.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#85BBF0;strokeColor=#5D82A8;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="570" y="120" width="440" height="105" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3aud" value="&lt;b&gt;audit.py — INV4 hash-chained audit&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;Append-only JSONL, each entry chained to the last. Records the active mode so attribution survives shared tool sets (ADR 017).&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#85BBF0;strokeColor=#5D82A8;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="570" y="242" width="440" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3ses" value="&lt;b&gt;session.py — INV5 resumability&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;· decisions.py · signing_keys.py (RS256) · jwks.py · oauth_verifier.py — the human accountability anchor behind `snodo authorize`&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#85BBF0;strokeColor=#5D82A8;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="570" y="338" width="440" height="80" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="f3cC" value="Run-time services" style="rounded=0;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#D0D0D0;dashed=1;verticalAlign=top;align=left;spacing=6;fontSize=11;fontColor=#999999;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1060" y="90" width="480" height="340" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3wt" value="&lt;b&gt;worktree.py&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;per-task git worktree isolation; base branch resolved from origin/HEAD; preserved on failure for inspection (ADR 025)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#85BBF0;strokeColor=#5D82A8;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="120" width="440" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3env" value="&lt;b&gt;environment.py&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;detects the ecosystem and runs a lockfile-frozen install in a fresh worktree; failure is an operational fault, not a judgement (ADR 024)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#85BBF0;strokeColor=#5D82A8;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="202" width="440" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3mr" value="&lt;b&gt;model_resolver / catalog / discovery&lt;/b&gt; &lt;font style=&quot;font-size:10px&quot;&gt;per-role model resolution (coder · validator · classifier), resolved once so model and api_base cannot diverge (ADR 020)&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#85BBF0;strokeColor=#5D82A8;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="284" width="440" height="70" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="f3misc" value="&lt;b&gt;wave_registry&lt;/b&gt; (task classification) · &lt;b&gt;usage_tracker&lt;/b&gt; (tokens + cost per call) · &lt;b&gt;memory&lt;/b&gt; (SqliteSaver) · &lt;b&gt;state&lt;/b&gt; · &lt;b&gt;cloud_sync&lt;/b&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#85BBF0;strokeColor=#5D82A8;verticalAlign=top;spacing=6;align=left;fontSize=10;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1080" y="366" width="440" height="52" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="f3inv" value="&lt;b&gt;Invariant → mechanism&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;INV1&lt;/b&gt; token integrity → TokenIssuer; JWT signed, and consumed at the dispatch boundary&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;INV2&lt;/b&gt; capability bounded by active mode → WorkspaceMCP / GitMCP path and operation validation, plus .snodo/ refusal (ADR 026) and the InPlaceCoderAdapter snapshot for coders that bypass the tool surface entirely (ADR 027)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;INV3&lt;/b&gt; non-overridable blockers → ConstraintEngine and policy aggregation&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;INV4&lt;/b&gt; audit hash-chain → append-only chained JSONL&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;INV5&lt;/b&gt; session resumability → SessionManager and the SqliteSaver checkpoint&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#E1D5E7;strokeColor=#9673A6;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="470" width="740" height="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>

        <mxCell id="f3rec" value="&lt;b&gt;What this layer got right — and it is the thing worth protecting&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Every defect found in a week of hard use was in the harness around this layer, never in the layer itself. Protocol compilation, capability binding, the audit chain and session resumability produced no incidents.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;The recurring defect shape is elsewhere and consistent:&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;a safety property degrading to a warning, or an operational fault reported as a judgement.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Corollary: the gates are the weak point, not the model of governance. Five were found reporting green while not gating — .importlinter, the e2e suite, ruff, check-bindings, and quality-versus-acceptance.&lt;/font&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#D5E8D4;strokeColor=#82B366;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;align=left;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="800" y="470" width="740" height="180" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
